  "sketch": "What each record CAN and CANNOT support, stated plainly:\n\n=== BASIL ===\nTemperature (29°C best of {11,17,23,29,35}, Walters & Currey 2019, Nufar, 3-week vegetative):\n  CAN: Show 'your air temp is near/far from what worked best for Nufar in a 3-week growth chamber trial'\n  CANNOT: Tell any basil grower their plant is healthy. Cannot say 35°C is lethal. Cannot say 29°C is optimal — 30 or 31 might be better. Cultivar-locked to Nufar.\n\nLight (500 PPFD 16h, Beaman et al. 2009, 3 cultivars):\n  CAN: Show reference point for controlled-environment edible biomass production under 16h photoperiod\n  CANNOT: Serve as a biological optimum — 600 PPFD produced the same biomass. The '500 not 600' recommendation is explicitly an energy-cost decision (unresolved_requirements includes '전력비 목적함수'). Cannot apply to other photoperiods. Cannot become a damage ceiling.\n\nRH (>=85% infection, >95% night sporulation, UConn Extension 2024):\n  CAN: Flag conditions favourable to downy mildew IF inoculum is present AND cultivar is susceptible\n  CANNOT: Say any RH is good for growth. Cannot fire as an instantaneous alarm. Cannot predict disease — only describes conditions for it. Score semantics explicitly pending.\n\n=== PEPPERMINT ===\nLight (150-200 PPFD 14h, Nagase et al. 2025, Mentha 3 spp including piperita):\n  CAN: Suggest a band that looked suitable in short-term potted trials with acknowledged replication limits\n  CANNOT: Confirm a definitive optimum — some within-species differences were not statistically significant (status: contextual_anchor_with_replication_limit). Cannot extend to long-term production or essential oil quality.\n\n=== WASABI ===\nTemperature (18/18°C, Hoang et al. 2020):\n  CAN: Nothing useful for a smart-farm grower. This is photoautotrophic micropropagation in an in-vitro culture system. The measurement_basis is '광독립영양 미세번식 배양의 주·야간 대기온도 처리' (day/night air temperature treatment of photoautotrophic micropropagation culture). The context.environment is 'in-vitro culture system'.\n  CANNOT: Apply to any production stage, even nursery plug production, because the growing system (culture vessels vs substrate) is fundamentally different. The brief's phrasing 'nursery stage only' is misleading — it is 'tissue culture only.'\n\nLight (140 PPFD 12h, wasabi Daruma, 2025):\n  CAN: Show that 140 was the best of {35,60,90,140} in a 44-week Daruma plant factory trial at 16-18°C, 68% RH\n  CANNOT: Claim 140 is optimal — the record's own status is 'highest_tested_not_bounded_optimum'. Cannot say anything above 140 is bad. Cannot apply outside Daruma cultivar at those specific environmental conditions.\n\n=== LETTUCE ===\nTemperature (23/18°C best of {15/10,23/18,30/23}, Zhou et al. 2022):\n  CAN: Show that in a factorial trial, this temperature regime was best, but ONLY in conjunction with stating which PPFD levels that applies to. The record's own interaction_note forbids separation.\n  CANNOT: Serve as an independent temperature normal range. A grower whose PPFD is 100 µmol/m²/s cannot be told 23/18°C is fine based on this study.\n\nLight DLI (11.5 mol/m²/d, Gavhane et al. 2023, Glendana iceberg, PPFD fixed at 200):\n  CAN: Serve as a DLI target for iceberg lettuce Glendana in vertical hydroponics with white LED at PPFD 200\n  CANNOT: Apply to other lettuce types (leaf, butterhead, romaine). Cannot separate 200 PPFD as independently optimal. Cultivar-locked.\n\n=== CORIANDER ===\nLight (200 PPFD 16h, Wang et al. 2024):\n  CAN: Show yield-and-energy-efficiency recommendation for fresh-leaf PFAL production\n  CANNOT: Serve as biological optimum — 400 PPFD was also tested and the recommendation encodes energy cost. Cannot apply the trial's fixed 24°C / 48% RH as optima (explicitly prohibited).\n\n=== CHERRY TOMATO, WELSH ONION, ARUGULA ===\n  CAN: Nothing. Zero verified records.\n  CANNOT: Support any environmental score on any crop axis.\n\n=== COMMON AXES (PM, NOISE) ===\n  CAN: Show human health reference values (WHO), Korean forecast classification, Korean alert thresholds, Korean noise standards.\n  CANNOT: Say anything about crop health. These protect people, not plants. PM readings cannot match WHO 24h/annual means from instantaneous values. Noise requires site zoning to select the correct row.\n\n=== BOTTOM LINE ===\nNot a single record in this corpus can honestly answer 'is my plant doing well?' The best records can answer 'is my environment near what a specific study found worked for a specific cultivar under specific conditions?' That is a fundamentally different claim.",

